  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Procurement Initiative: Procurement Assistance Program for the Dominican Republic: Phases I and II, through Trade Center Management Associates LLC</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Global Procurement Initiative: Procurement Assistance Program for the Dominican Republic: Phases I and II is a national-level Program that encompasses two separate and distinct activities: a three-day Phase I Workshop in Santo Domingo for 60-80 government procurement officials and up to 20 observers in the October 2017 timeframe; and a Phase II value-based procurement Phase II Study Tour in early 2018. Both activities are to be carried out in collaboration with the Direccion General de Contrataciones Publicas (DGCP), the George Washington University Law School&apos;s Government Procurement Law Program (GW) and USTDA&apos;s GPI technical specialists. This funding in the amount of $22,464 is being added to a logistics contract to provide funding for an IQC contractor to support USTDA&apos;s Global Procurement Initiative: Understanding Best Value (GPI) Procurement Assistance Program for the Dominican Republic Phases I and II. This funding in the amount of $37702 is being added to a logistics contract to provide funding for the IQC contractor to support three (3) more delegates and one (1) additional staff member to support USTDA&apos;s Global Procurement Initiative (GPI) Procurement Assistance Program for Dominican Republic: Phase II Study Tour.</narrative>
  </description>
